  {
   "id": 42,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    -2000,
    -720
   ],
   "size": [
    460,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 41,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "MC SEQUENCE \u2014 30\u201390 s anti-drift chaining (SVI 2.0 Pro)\n\nWHAT THIS DOES\nChains Wan 2.2 I2V A14B segments with the Stable-Video-Infinity\n2.0 Pro LoRAs. Every segment is conditioned on the SAME anchor\nlatent (your start image) \u2014 identity cannot walk away over the\nchain. Motion continuity comes from each segment's last frame,\nColorMatched back to the anchor before hand-off, so color cannot\nwalk either.\n\nTHIS FILE = 3 segments \u00d7 81 frames @ 16 fps \u2248 15 s per queue.\nFor 30\u201390 s: duplicate the SEGMENT 2 group (it contains the full\nhand-off chain) \u2014 see note \u2465. Each extra segment adds ~5 s:\n30 s \u2248 6 segments \u00b7 90 s \u2248 18 segments. The fixed anchor keeps\nidentity locked no matter how many you add.\n\nQUICK START\n1) Download the 2 SVI Pro LoRAs \u2014 note \u2461. REQUIRED.\n2) INPUT group: upload your 9:16 start image.\n3) Write SEGMENT 1/2/3 prompts (rules in note \u2462).\n4) Queue. Output \u2192 output/mc_sequence/.\n\n~4\u20136 min per segment on A100 80GB @ 480\u00d7832, 20 steps."
   ],
   "title": "\u2460 READ ME \u2014 MC SEQUENCE",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 43,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    -1500,
    -720
   ],
   "size": [
    460,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 42,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "ALREADY ON VOLUME\ndiffusion_models/wan2.2_i2v_high_noise_14B_fp8_scaled.safetensors\ndiffusion_models/wan2.2_i2v_low_noise_14B_fp8_scaled.safetensors\ntext_encoders/umt5_xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors\nvae/wan_2.1_vae.safetensors\nloras/wan2.2_i2v_lightx2v_4steps_lora_v1_{high,low}_noise.safetensors\n\nNEW DOWNLOAD \u2014 REQUIRED (~2.4 GB total; the chain does not work\nwithout them):\nloras/SVI_v2_PRO_Wan2.2-I2V-A14B_HIGH_lora_rank_128_fp16.safetensors\nloras/SVI_v2_PRO_Wan2.2-I2V-A14B_LOW_lora_rank_128_fp16.safetensors\nSource: huggingface.co/Kijai/WanVideo_comfy\n        \u2192 LoRAs/Stable-Video-Infinity/v2.0/  (1.23 GB each, fp16)\ncd models/loras && wget https://huggingface.co/Kijai/WanVideo_comfy/resolve/main/LoRAs/Stable-Video-Infinity/v2.0/SVI_v2_PRO_Wan2.2-I2V-A14B_HIGH_lora_rank_128_fp16.safetensors\nwget .../SVI_v2_PRO_Wan2.2-I2V-A14B_LOW_lora_rank_128_fp16.safetensors\n\nWHY fp16: fp16 accumulates less error over long chains (SVI only\nships fp16 \u2014 good). Volume UNETs are fp8_scaled: fine for 3\nsegments; fp16 UNETs are cleaner for very long chains but ~2\u00d7\nsize/VRAM.\n\nSTACK ORDER (both experts): UNET \u2192 Character LoRA \u2192 SVI Pro \u2192\nLightning \u2192 shift. Keep HIGH files on the HIGH expert, LOW on\nLOW \u2014 crossing them breaks sampling."
   ],
   "title": "\u2461 MODELS + NEW DOWNLOAD",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 44,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    -1000,
    -720
   ],
   "size": [
    460,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 43,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "HOW THE CHAIN WORKS\nanchor latent = VAEEncode(start image) \u2192 EVERY segment's\n  anchor_samples (identity anchor \u2014 the anti-drift core).\nprev context  = segment N last frame \u2192 ColorMatch (vs anchor)\n  \u2192 VAEEncode \u2192 segment N+1 prev_samples\n  (motion_latent_count 1).\n\nPROMPT RULES (titles are the patch contract)\nEach segment prompt = STATE + MOTION:\n  STATE  \u2014 what is already true when the segment starts\n  MOTION \u2014 what happens during these 81 frames\n\nOFF-FRAME ENTRIES go in the NEXT segment's prompt, never the\ncurrent one. Example (already wired into SEGMENT 2's prompt):\n\"a hand enters from the right and gives her a drink\" \u2014 anything\nentering frame must be introduced at a segment boundary, in the\nsegment where it appears.\n\nKeep character, outfit, scene and lighting descriptions\nIDENTICAL across all segments \u2014 contradicting the anchor is\ndrift you asked for. Only STATE and MOTION should change."
   ],
   "title": "\u2462 CHAINING + PROMPT RULES",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 45,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
