   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 44,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "81 FRAMES PER SEGMENT IS A HARD LIMIT\n121-frame segments = progressive color degradation (latent\nsaturation walk). Never raise length \u2014 add segments instead.\n\nSLOW MOTION + COLOR SHIFT ACROSS THE CHAIN\n#1 cause: lightning/distill LoRAs. They are BYPASSED here on\npurpose and pre-set to 0.6 strength. Draft mode: enable both,\nsteps 6, cfg 1.0, shift 5.0 \u2014 expect softer joins. Never render\nfinal chains with them enabled.\n\nIDENTITY STILL DRIFTS \u2192 enable Character LoRA on BOTH experts\n(strength 0.6\u20130.9) and/or use a cleaner, sharper anchor still.\n\nVISIBLE JUMP AT A JOIN \u2192 set motion_latent_count 2 on the next\nsegment AND num_frames 5 on the tail LAST FRAME node, or drop\nColorMatch strength to 0.7.\n\nSATURATION CREEP AFTER MANY SEGMENTS \u2192 switch ColorMatch method\nmkl \u2192 hm-mkl-hm.\n\nOOM at 480\u00d7832\u00d781f \u2192 replace VAEDecode with VAEDecodeTiled, or\nset UNET weight_dtype fp8_e4m3fn_fast."
   ],
   "title": "\u2463 FAILURE MODES + FIXES",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 46,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    0,
    -720
   ],
   "size": [
    460,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 45,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "GENERATE AT 480\u00d7832 (9:16) \u2014 ALWAYS.\nChains run ~3\u00d7 faster than at 720\u00d71280, drift-per-step is\nlower, and 81 frames fits VRAM comfortably. Generation size\ncomes from the anchor ImageScale node \u2014 do not raise it.\n\nUPSCALE AFTER APPROVAL, on the finished mp4:\n480\u00d7832 \u2192 1080\u00d71920 with your upscaler of choice (SeedVR2 /\nTopaz / a Wan low-noise refine pass). Upscaling drafts burns\n10\u00d7 GPU time on takes you will throw away.\n\nFPS: segments render 16 fps native (81f = 5.06 s each).\nRIFE \u00d72 \u2192 32 fps export. For a 24 fps deliverable: RIFE\nmultiplier 3 (\u2192 48 fps) + frame_rate 48, or remove RIFE and\nexport at 16."
   ],
   "title": "\u2464 VERTICAL 480\u00d7832 + UPSCALE-AFTER POLICY",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 47,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    500,
    -720
   ],
   "size": [
    460,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 46,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "SEGMENT 2 and SEGMENT 3 are boxed for exactly this:\n\n10 s RUN \u2014 select the SEGMENT 3 group frame \u2192 Ctrl+B.\nIts CONCAT node is bypassed too and passes S1+S2 straight\nthrough to RIFE.\n 5 s RUN \u2014 bypass BOTH the SEGMENT 2 and SEGMENT 3 groups.\nNever bypass Seg 2 while keeping Seg 3: segment 3's prev\ncontext comes from segment 2's tail \u2014 the chain breaks.\n\nSEEDS are fixed and different per segment (77710001 /\n77720002 / 77730003) so a prompt set reproduces exactly.\nChange all three for a new take. Same seed on every segment\nmakes repetitive motion \u2014 keep them different.\n\nEXTENDING PAST 15 s \u2014 duplicate the SEGMENT 2 group (it has\nthe full tail hand-off), then rewire on the copy:\n  SVI prev_samples \u2190 previous segment's tail VAEEncode\n  SVI anchor_samples \u2190 ANCHOR LATENT (never changes)\n  CONCAT images_A \u2190 previous CONCAT IMAGE output\n  new fixed seed on the HIGH sampler\n+5 s per copy. 30 s \u2248 6 segments \u00b7 90 s \u2248 18 segments."
   ],
   "title": "\u2465 SHORT RUNS \u00b7 SEEDS \u00b7 EXTENDING",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
 ],
